# D-061. commander and yargs spell the call .option(flags, description), so the
# description is the second POSITIONAL argument and no `name=` keyword ends the
# scan. Both literals were mined for flags, so this tree published --keep, -x
# and --purge -- and doctype.py folds user_surface.commands into the allowlist
# its flag lens is suppressed by, so a user page backticking `--purge` passed,
# excused by a flag the product does not have.
#
# Line 2 of the same file is the control: commander's "-o, --out <path>" is one
# literal holding two spellings and a value placeholder, and it is a real
# declaration. Ending the positional run at the first literal that is not a
# pure flag spec must not end it there.

